  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason — the skewness of the lotteries — is not considered by the individual. The individual does not mention or evaluate the distribution of probabilities, nor do they refer to unfavorable outcomes having greater weight. Instead, they focus on the higher probability of a large gain in B (0.1% vs 0.2%) and the perception of luck. The decision reason requires an evaluation of skewness (i.e., whether one lottery has more probability mass on unfavorable outcomes), which is absent from the report. The individual’s justification is based on a different criterion — the chance of a large gain — not on skewness. Therefore, the decision reason was not used in the deliberation process. The individual’s reasoning is inconsistent with the rule of the decision reason, which would require comparing the asymmetry of the probability distribution. Hence, the decision reason was not applied.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
